The '''Grand Salon''', also called the '''Sundari throne room''', was a vast chamber within the [[Sundari Royal Palace]] in [[Sundari]], [[Mandalore]]. It served many functions, primarily as [[Duchess]] [[Satine Kryze]]'s throne room, but also as a council chamber.

==Description==
The vast<ref name="MandalorePlot" /> Grand Salon<ref name="CoR" /> chamber, also known as the Sundari [[throne room]],<ref name="Ahsoka vs Maul">''[[The Clone Wars: Ahsoka vs. Maul]]''</ref> was the seat of [[Mandalorian]] power during the [[Standard day|days]] of the late [[Republic Era]]. Located within the [[capital]] [[city]] of [[Sundari]] on the [[planet]] [[Mandalore]], the room saw use by [[Duchess]] [[Satine Kryze]], the reigning monarch of the pacificist [[New Mandalorians]].<ref name="MandalorePlot" /> When the [[Mandalorian Government Council]] was in session, they sat in chairs arranged before the throne.<ref name="Corruption">{{TCW|Corruption (episode)}}</ref> The [[terrorist]] and [[Mandalorian warrior|warrior-based]] [[Death Watch]] Mandalorians later [[Takeover of Mandalore|claimed control]] over Mandalore, with Death Watch leader [[Pre Vizsla]] claiming the Grand Salon in the process. When the rogue [[Sith Lord]] [[Maul]] then took over Death Watch from Vizsla, he continued to make use of the Grand Salon, reigning as ruler of Mandalore from the throne room<ref name="ShadesOfReason" /> and also standing as leader of the [[Shadow Collective]] criminal alliance.<ref name="OldFriends" />

==History==
[[File:UnlimitedTwilight-Maul.png|thumb|left|300px|Maul claimed control of Mandalore and ruled from the throne room.]]
During the [[Clone Wars]], due to Mandalore's status as neutral ground, the Grand Salon housed a [[Confederate–Republic peace conference|failed attempt]] at an accord between the leaders of the [[Galactic Republic]] and the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] to end the conflict.<ref name="CoR" /> As the seat of Mandalorian power, the throne room was the location for a number of duels and skirmishes as various factions jostled for control of Mandalore<ref name="Lawless" /> after Death Watch's takeover<ref name="ShadesOfReason" /> in [[19 BBY]].<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> First, it was the site of a duel between Maul and Pre Viszla that ended in Maul claiming control over the world.<ref name="ShadesOfReason" /> Later, Satine was killed there by Maul in front of [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]]. Shortly after Satine's death, [[Darth Sidious]] arrived on Mandalore, when he engaged in a duel with Maul and [[Savage Opress]], killing Opress then defeating and capturing his former apprentice.<ref name="Lawless">{{TCW|The Lawless}}</ref>

In [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines" /> Maul returned to Mandalore after being freed from captivity by [[Mandalorian super commando]]s; however, he hid out in the [[Undercity]] and left his governing puppet, [[Prime Minister]] [[Almec]], in the throne room. During the [[Siege of Mandalore]], the [[Nite Owls]] infiltrated the throne room and captured Almec there.<ref name="OldFriends" /> Maul and [[Ahsoka Tano]] dueled in the throne room, before continuing their fight in the rafters of the city dome.<ref name="PhantomApprentice">{{TCW|The Phantom Apprentice}}</ref>

